    81	Materials and methods
    82	
    83	Study population. This study was a cross-sectional study in which after obtaining informed consent from
    84	participants, 100 samples were collected from lactating women living in urban areas of Kermanshah city during
    85	September to December 2021. This research was funded by Kermanshah University of Medical Sciences (ethic
    86	code: IR.KUMS.REC.1399.222). Participants were healthy breastfeeding mothers who were primiparous and
    87	breastfeed only one child after a normal pregnancy with no complications. They were residence of Kermanshah
    88	for at least five years. Mothers with chronic pre-pregnancy diseases (cardiac or autoimmune diseases) and also
    89	those living in areas with known emissions or suspected to the elevated levels of pollutants were ­excluded6.
    90	Breast milk sample collection. The health center’s staff carried out all sampling procedures according to
    91	the study protocols. After the admission of lactating women to the study, 5 to 10 ml of milk was collected during morning hours by manual expression from each person. Mothers were instructed to wash their hands and
    92	chest areas before collecting samples. Collected samples were labeled inside sterile polyethylene tubes. The milk
    93	samples were then kept at − 20 °C until further ­analyses31.
    94	Drinking water. In this study, the volume of water used was 5 cc. The sample locations were in Kermanshah
    95	city and similarly at the same time as the samples of mothers’ milk. We used sterilized plastic bottles that had
    96	already been washed with distilled water and 20% Nitric acid ­(HNO3). For sampling, the tap water was opened
    97	for few seconds to make sure the municipal water network is collected. To prevent adsorption and crystallization
    98	of the trace element, water samples were then filtered using a 0.45 mm Whatman’s membrane and acidified with
    99	3 ml of nitric acid ­(HNO3, 65%, Merck, Germany)32. Samples were then transferred to cool, dark containers and
   100	kept at 4 °C until Inductively coupled plasma mass spectrometry (ICP-MS) analyses.
   101	Heavy metals/metalloids in water and milk measurements. To prepare milk samples for digestion,
