   503	
   504	4 Conclusion
   505	Overall, all the samples in this study showed a high content
   506	of the essential minerals assessed, especially iron, chromium
   507	and manganese. Two samples (1 and 2), in particular, from two
   508	different locations in Rio Grande do Sul State (Brazil), were found
   509	to be suitable sources of these minerals. Because contamination
   510	can occur as a result of improper use of pesticides, fertilizers and
   511	other chemicals in agriculture, careful handling and frequent
   512	monitoring are essential to ensure food safety.
