   744	The results for TCR calculated from Eq. 3 are shown in Table 3. The target cancer risk was calculated only
   745	for As, Cd, and Pb because the CPSo value was only calculated for these metals while the other metals Fe, Zn,
   746	and Mn have no CPSo value so the TCR value was not calculated for the TCR value for Pb as found 0.002862
   747	or 2.8 ×10−3, for Cd its value was 0.016 or 1.6 ×10−2 and for As the TCR was calculated 0.028 or 2.8 ×10−2. The
   748	highest value was calculated for As 0.028 or 2.8 ×10−2, while the lowest found for Pb was 0.002862 or 3.8 ×10−3 .
   749	
   750	Discussion
   751	
   752	Throughout the world, pollution of water with HMs is the main ­problem58. HMs is the most toxic source of water
   753	pollution in the river Punjkora. Most of the heavy metals in the water were above the permissible limits of that
   754	prescribed by WHO and Pak-EPA. The results show that the concentration of HMs in water such as Fe and As
   755	were detected less as compared to Pb, Mn, Zn, and Cd. The concentration of Fe was 0.01 mg/L in Sheringal Khall
   756	and Thall while in Wari, Bosaq, Shagokas and Timergara the concentration of Fe was not detected. The value of
   757	Fe was high in the tributaries of the river was 0.02 mg/L in Dir River and Gumber. The average concentration of
   758	Fe in upstream and downstream were 0.56 and 0.96 mg/L in the water of Tembi ­River59. The concentration of As
   759	was not detected in Bosaq and Shagokas and the concentration of As was 0.04 and 0.03 mg/L in Kunai Khwar
   760	and Gumbir tributaries. In Bangladesh Korotoa River, the concentration of As was 46 mg/L60.

